{"t": 160.976, "n": 109, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the task rows for all five phases and the proof table into `plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i21b.plan.md`. Nothing has been run, since this step has no shell. The status is still `planned`, and sections 0, 1 and 4, the phase names, the goals and the weights are unchanged. I ran no git, so I did not commit the plan, and the engine commits it when this step ends.\n\n- **Rows:** There are 21 rows across the five phases. In each phase a `test` row comes before the `code` row it covers, and each test row names the spec criterion it proves.\n  - Phase 1 (the flag refusal) has rows 1.1 to 1.5.\n  - Phase 2 (the preflight refusal of undefined servers) has rows 2.1 to 2.4.\n  - Phase 3 (the launch refusal) has rows 3.1 to 3.5.\n  - Phase 4 (the live probe) has rows 4.1 to 4.3.\n  - Phase 5 (the record) has rows 5.1 to 5.4.\n- **Requirements and docs:** Every requirement R1 to R7 is named by at least one row. The one document under Docs to update, `live-checks.plan.md`, has a `docs` row (5.4). No row was marked complete.\n- **Verification:** I kept the three existing commands and added four single-file pytest commands. The proof table has one row for each of AC 1 to AC 6, each with a test file and the command that runs it.\n\nI made four design choices where the plan was silent:\n- **Flag refusal:** the probe puts `missing_flags` in its facts, and preflight reads that to name the flag. `ProbeReport` and `ProbeWord` keep their shape.\n- **Preflight check:** `ClaudeExecutor` gets an optional `undefined_mcp_servers` method that preflight looks up by name, so stand-in executors are untouched. Preflight reads the operator's configuration from the current working folder, because it has no worktree path.\n- **Launch refusal:** a refused launch returns `ok=False` with `error_kind=\"refused\"` and the reason in `text`, so no new `SessionResult` field is added. I did not check how the retry and tool-access escalation paths treat `\"refused\"`, so the code step should look at that.\n- **Live-probe helper:** the helper lives in `tests/fixtures/mcp_turns.py` so it imports offline, and its tests are in `tests/test_mcp_turns.py`.\n\nTwo proof-table entries are weaker than the spec's wording:\n- **AC 3 and AC 6:** the AC 3 and AC 6 proof rows point at `test_preflight.py`. The launch refusal (ECC-AC18) is tested in `test_claude_executor.py`, and that file is not in the proof table.\n- **Exit code 2:** the preflight tests check the refusal on the report. They do not run the command to check exit code 2.\n\nARTIFACT phases: plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i21b.plan.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "99a2b69a-6771-4e83-b179-469d2d74a7ab"}
